 World in Quantum Theory", "author": "Joos,", "year": "1996"}, {"key": "2022081219332695800_", "volume-title": "Classical Charged Particles", "author": "Rohrlich,", "year": "1965"}, {"key": "2022081219332695800_", "volume-title": "The Quantum Theory of Fields", "author": "Weinberg,", "year": "1995"}, {"key": "2022081219332695800_", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/RevModPhys.17.157", "article-title": "Interaction with the absorber as the mechanism of radiation.", "author": "Wheeler,", "year": "1945"}, {"key": "2022081219332695800_", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/RevModPhys.21.425", "article-title": "Classical electrodynamics in terms of direct interparticle action.", "author": "Wheeler,", "year": "1949"}], "container-title": ["The Theory of Open Quantum Systems"], "language": "en", "link": [{"URL": "https://academic.oup.com/book/chapter-pdf/44603234/book_27757_section_197984340.ag.pdf", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2022, 8, 12]], "date-time": "2022-08-12T19:40:40Z", "timestamp": 1660333240000}, "score": 52.455517, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://academic.oup.com/book/27757/chapter/197984340"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2007, 1, 25]]}, "ISBN": ["0199213909", "9780199213900", "9780191706349"], "references-count": 22, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199213900.003.12", "published": {"date-parts": [[2007, 1, 25]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2024, 4, 29]], "date-time": "2024-04-29T04:40:10Z", "timestamp": 1714365610892}, "edition-number": "1", "reference-count": 21, "publisher": "Oxford University PressOxford", "isbn-type": [{"value": "0199213909", "type": "print"}, {"value": "9780199213900", "type": "print"}, {"value": "9780191706349", "type": "electronic"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2007, 1, 25]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n               <jats:p>This chapter develops the fundamental notions and concepts of the probabilistic and statistical interpretation of quantum mechanics. It begins with a brief review of the mathematical structure given by a Hilbert space of state vectors and an algebra of observables represented by selfadjoint operators. Special emphasis is laid on the connection between the spectral representation of a selfadjoint operator and a corresponding random variable that describes the possible measurement outcomes. The chapter further introduces the concepts of a composite quantum system, of the reduced density matrix, and of entangled quantum states. A section on quantum entropies is included, as well as the mathematical formulation of the generalized theory of quantum measurements in terms of completely positive quantum operations and effects.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199213900.003.02", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2010, 1, 20]], "date-time": "2010-01-20T08:30:40Z", "timestamp": 1263976240000}, "page": "59-106", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Quantum Probability"], "prefix": "10.1093", "author": [{"given": "Heinz-Peter", "family": "Breuer", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Francesco", "family": "Petruccione", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "286", "reference": [{"key": "2022081219332695800_", "volume-title": "Theory of Linear Operators in Hilbert Space", "author": "Akhiezer,", "year": "1981"}, {"key": "2022081219332695800_", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/RevModPhys.68.755", "article-title": "On the measurement of a weak classical force coupled to a harmonic oscillator: Experimental progress.", "author": "Bocko,", "year": "1996"}, {"key": "2022081219332695800_", "volume-title": "Quantum Mechanics", "author": "